  "body": "I think that we have the property that \r\n\r\n> Given the set of tuple origins that can be produced by the [URL origin algorithm](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-origin), every ASCII string is the [serialization](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#ascii-serialisation-of-an-origin) of at most one of them.\r\n\r\n@martinthomson pointed out that we never actually say that anywhere, and maybe we should so that any future schemes preserve the property. And, if it's not actually the case, we should probably say that too, so silly people like me don't rely on it incorrectly.",
